course: dictionary
lesson: 9023
title: Skydiver
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A skydiver is a person who jumps out of an aeroplane high up, falls through the air, and then opens a parachute to land safely. Skydive is the verb, the action of doing this. Skydiving is the sport.
explain: Read the words around skydiver to work out its meaning. «Skydivers spread out like a starfish to catch more air» tells you they are falling through the air. «A parachute's big cloth catches lots of air» tells you the parachute is what slows them down.
explain: Some words paint a picture. «Dive head first like an arrow» means straight and fast, with the body pointing down. Like a starfish means spread wide. The writer uses these pictures to show how a skydiver moves.
fact: A skydiver jumps out of an aeroplane and falls through the air.
fact: A parachute opens to catch air and slow the skydiver down.
fact: «Skydiving» is the sport, and «skydive» is the verb: to jump and fall this way.
fact: Without a parachute a skydiver falls at about 200 kilometres an hour.
fact: With the parachute open, the landing is about as hard as jumping off a low wall.
exercise: «Skydivers spread out like a starfish to catch more air.» What does spread out mean here? | Fall asleep | Hide under a cloud | *Open wide | Land on one foot
exercise: What is a skydiver? | A machine that makes parachutes | A person who lands in a tree | *A person who jumps from a plane, falls, then opens a parachute to land safely | A pilot who flies aeroplanes over the sea
exercise: «With the parachute open, the landing is about as hard as jumping off a low wall.» What does this tell you? | The landing is as hard as falling from a tall tree | The parachute stops the skydiver from landing at all | *The parachute makes the landing much gentler | The parachute makes the skydiver fall faster
test: Which word is the verb for the action of jumping and falling this way? | *skydive | skydiver | skydivers | skydiving
test: «A parachute's big cloth catches lots of air.» What does a parachute do? | It lights up the sky | *It catches air to slow the fall | It carries the aeroplane home | It makes the skydiver fall faster
exam: Which is the best meaning of skydiver? | A sport played with a ball and a net | A worker who packs boxes in a factory | A bird that glides over the hills | *Someone who jumps from a plane high up, then uses a parachute to land safely
